  "body": "In the file `./cpp/non_iid_main.cpp`, line 139 ensures that the length of the binary string doesn't go beyond 1,000,000 symbols if flag `-t` is enabled, i.e.:\r\n\r\n```\r\nif(!all_bits && (data.blen > MIN_SIZE)) data.blen = MIN_SIZE;\r\n```\r\n\r\nHowever, there doesn't seem to be any line that provides a similar option in the non-binary case. To verify this, I ran the non-IID track twice on the same dataset of 8-bit words: once using the `-t` flag and once using the `-a` flag. As expected, I got the exact same results both time. What I suggest is to add a single line of code as follows:\r\n\r\n```\r\nif(!all_bits && (data.len > MIN_SIZE)) data.len = MIN_SIZE;\r\n```",
